                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4e7f64f3-2101-479d-9382-226e5390e0f2",
                        "entry_id": "e4eed703-fdce-3319-b405-b66c2484c21e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "damasten"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0dfa27de-acf8-3f01-90d7-20bafa02b8a4",
                        "entry_id": "e4eed703-fdce-3319-b405-b66c2484c21e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "weeftechniek, waarbij tekeningen aangebracht worden op een achtergrond van dezelfde kleur"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c29ae13f-c7c8-4331-9e50-e8780e7b6444",
                                "sense_id": "0dfa27de-acf8-3f01-90d7-20bafa02b8a4",
                                "text": "Het Drents Museum in Assen heeft een schenking van bijna 25.000 stukken gekregen. Het gaat om de collectie van de Stichting Schone Kunsten rond 1900 (SSK 1900). De verzameling, uiteenlopend van schilderijen en meubelontwerpen tot serviezen en damast, omvat onder meer werk van Chris Lebeau, Bart van der Leck en H.P. Berlage. De Stichting Schone Kunsten rond 1900 werd opgericht in 1964 en verzamelde in Nederland ontstane beeldende kunst en kunstnijverheid uit de periode 1885-1935, maar wordt nu opgeheven. SSK 1900 was indertijd een initiatief van naaste familieleden van de kunstenaars. In korte tijd brachten die geheel belangeloos kunstwerken en documenten bijeen. In 1974 werden die in bruikleen gegeven aan het Drents Museum. Nadien is de collectie nog aanzienlijk uitgebreid."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5bc31546-c66e-408a-be38-d2ee51bde355",
                                "sense_id": "0dfa27de-acf8-3f01-90d7-20bafa02b8a4",
                                "text": "Dit stilleven (c. 1610, 65 x 85 cm) van Osias Beert toont de stoffelijke wereld tot in het kleinste detail. Tegelijkertijd laat het zien dat deze wereld niet meer is dan een efemere zinsbegoocheling - of een dunne laag verf. Stillevens gaan niet alleen over de dingen die erop zijn afgebeeld, maar evengoed over de handeling van het schilderen zelf. Neem de stillevens van Floris van Dijck (Haarlem, 1675-1651), waar behalve gestapelde kazen vooral tafellakens de aandacht vragen. Minutieus schilderde Van Dijck vogels en bloemen geweven in glanzend damast. Scherp gevouwen en in allerlei schakeringen van wit en grijs ligt het linnen damast gedrapeerd op een dun, roodwollen tafellaken."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "88bb3495-647e-43b7-8f8c-3a29fba96ea9",
                        "source_entry_id": "e4eed703-fdce-3319-b405-b66c2484c21e",
                        "source_sense_id": "0dfa27de-acf8-3f01-90d7-20bafa02b8a4",
                        "source_sense_description": "weeftechniek, waarbij tekeningen aangebracht worden op een achtergrond van dezelfde kleur",
                        "target_lang_word": "damask",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "damask",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b31b284-7b25-3ebc-8ec8-0fb7647b5100",
                                        "entry_id": "87c434e5-2fc4-328e-8e57-e55240cb8843",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ornate silk fabric originating from Damascus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79df308e-db82-40fc-ae47-ec356e90104a",
                                                "sense_id": "2b31b284-7b25-3ebc-8ec8-0fb7647b5100",
                                                "text": "True damasks are pure silk."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "920e6d73-6888-4831-bf3f-b9ce95acfeb6",
                                                "sense_id": "2b31b284-7b25-3ebc-8ec8-0fb7647b5100",
                                                "text": "[…]but what struck Tom's fancy most was a strange, grim-looking, high backed chair, carved in the most fantastic manner, with a flowered damask cushion, and the round knobs at the bottom of the legs carefully tied up in red cloth, as if it had got the gout in its toes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a5e6b26-b694-33f6-b72b-be1be6bee738",
                                        "entry_id": "87c434e5-2fc4-328e-8e57-e55240cb8843",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Linen so woven that a pattern is produced by the different directions of the thread, without contrast of colour."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a6abd871-f65e-3035-857c-ae90dbea6f4a",
                                        "entry_id": "87c434e5-2fc4-328e-8e57-e55240cb8843",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A heavy woolen or worsted stuff with a pattern woven in the same way as the linen damask; made for furniture covering and hangings."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a71203bb-d582-486d-9f5a-cf75a39015c7",
                                                "sense_id": "a6abd871-f65e-3035-857c-ae90dbea6f4a",
                                                "text": "Thus the red damask curtains which now shut out the fog-laden, drizzling atmosphere of the Marylebone Road, had cost a mere song, and yet they might have been warranted to last another thirty years. A great bargain also had been the excellent Axminster carpet which covered the floor; as, again, the arm-chair in which Bunting now sat forward, staring into the dull, small fire."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1618fd49-f169-3d99-a9c0-c4b019425630",
                                        "entry_id": "87c434e5-2fc4-328e-8e57-e55240cb8843",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Damascus steel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "067fb056-f30c-3c4c-aca2-cc4d6a3249a9",
                                        "entry_id": "87c434e5-2fc4-328e-8e57-e55240cb8843",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The peculiar markings or water of such steel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "271bede6-93e7-3231-95e7-4ebca4aedca6",
                                        "entry_id": "87c434e5-2fc4-328e-8e57-e55240cb8843",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A damask rose, Rosa × damascena."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a4d2a3d-8bce-3205-88e6-d94db6430684",
                                        "entry_id": "87c434e5-2fc4-328e-8e57-e55240cb8843",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A grayish-pink color, like that of the damask rose."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bdcb49fd-6a1c-4211-bb76-fade479b6eb8",
                                                "sense_id": "8a4d2a3d-8bce-3205-88e6-d94db6430684",
                                                "text": "Thursday. D. certainly improved. Better night. Slight tinge of damask revisiting cheek."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "damask",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e5f19713-969c-3787-88b9-81a989f26c54",
                                        "entry_id": "7c1f7f3b-7afb-3968-a3c4-707c30ff733b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a grayish-pink color, like that of the damask rose."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5cc2c6d2-3c6a-4c08-b643-63874adea5d5",
                                                "sense_id": "e5f19713-969c-3787-88b9-81a989f26c54",
                                                "text": "My cage has many rooms / Damask and dark / Nothing there sings, / Not even my lark."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cae7c1a2-f244-4c02-b1cf-8400bcf5e2d9",
                                                "sense_id": "e5f19713-969c-3787-88b9-81a989f26c54",
                                                "text": "But let concealment, like a worm i' the bud, / Feed on her damask cheek"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "478c66c6-303b-4582-ac44-a418f105c1bb",
                                                "sense_id": "e5f19713-969c-3787-88b9-81a989f26c54",
                                                "text": "They had a lurking suspicion even, that he died of secret love; though I must say there was a picture of him in the house with a damask nose, which concealment did not appear to have ever preyed upon."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "damask",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "30ff475c-5038-309d-81ba-74e99cef687e",
                                        "entry_id": "1ec900ee-4b60-39e4-8edc-84d988395d48",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To decorate or weave in damascene patterns"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b25a507-5e81-4958-bbb6-c60e5e351736",
                                                "sense_id": "30ff475c-5038-309d-81ba-74e99cef687e",
                                                "text": "Madame de Mercœur had herself arranged her dress, which was splendid white silk, damasked with silver flowers; but it was with much internal misgiving that she put on the graceful cap and plume."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
